        "original_id": "8ef3dd1c-4967-5d26-a2bd-a842cf80b5cf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Annette Crosbie, David Rintoul, Ian Bannen\n- Works: The Six Wives of Henry VIII, Edward the Seventh, The Slipper and the Rose, Doctor Finlay\n- Awards: BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress, BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role\n- Organizations: ITV\n\nFacts:\n- In 1971, Annette Crosbie won the BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress for The Six Wives of Henry VIII.\n- In 1976, Annette Crosbie won the BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress for Edward the Seventh.\n- In 1976, The Slipper and the Rose was released as a British musical film retelling the fairy tale Cinderella.\n- In 1976, Annette Crosbie was nominated for the BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role for The Slipper and the Rose.\n- ITV later returned Dr. Finlay to television with Doctor Finlay, which continued the stories into the late 1940s.\n- Doctor Finlay featured David Rintoul as Dr. Finlay, Ian Bannen as Dr. Cameron, and Annette Crosbie as Janet.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
